  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-172166",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $4$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n4=\\frac{4}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{4}{5}$ is $\\frac{5}{4}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n4÷\\frac{4}{5}=\\frac{4}{1}÷\\frac{4}{5}=\\frac{4}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. \n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{4}=\\frac{4\\times 5}{1\\times 4}=\\frac{20}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n20÷4=5\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
